        {
          "label": "Decrypt-only via WIF, drop nix-key later",
          "description": "Ship the .sops.yaml edit (host-key only) but DO NOT rewrap secrets.yaml this round. Bootstrap continues with nix-key still in the recipient set, but every wifHost will go down the WIF path at decrypt time because that's what the per-host config points at. nix-key stays as belt-and-braces until you can do the rewrap in a separate audit. Lower risk, but the file naming is dirtier."
